eys explicitly, and every rejection path emits to stderr and exits 2. The origin/main pin is correctly implemented — mktemp creates a mode-0600 exclusive file, the trap ensures cleanup, and the on.pull_request.branches:[main] trigger constrains base; branch protection (enforce_admins=true, required_signatures=true) prevents force-push to main. No CRIT runtime bypass path confirmed.\\\\n\\\\nOne MAJ gap: 024B-extras-3 is absent from both the workflow's tooling-slice exemption case statement (yml:72–80) and the enforcer script's --tooling-slice-id allowlist (check-invocation-log-entry.sh:213, 237). The slice's own PR modifies STATUS.md, which triggers the workflow. The resolve-dispatch step finds the 024B-extras-3 DISPATCH-NOTE, does not match the exempt list, sets enforce=true, and invokes the enforcer without --allow-not-applicable. The enforcer reads cascade-status: not applicable and dies (exit 2, line 199). CI fails on the slice's own merge commit. This is overcorrect (fail-closed, not a bypass) but reveals a dual-maintenance surface: if the workflow exempt list is updated for a future tooling slice without updating the enforcer allowlist, the workflow short-circuits enforcement while manual invocations diverge — a latent bypass path documented by FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001 but not closed by this slice.\\\\n\\\\nThree MIN findings address type-inconsistency in enforce_admins.enabled (lenient int 0/1 vs strict bool for toggle keys), a no-else silent-drop in transform() for TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS (not reachable today but a defense-in-depth gap), and bool() coercion in the required_signatures inline extraction that can mis-classify a string 'false' as enabled=true. One nit on test diagnostic coverage.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"024B-extras-3 is absent from both the workflow tooling-exempt case statement (yml:72–80) and the enforcer --tooling-slice-id allowlist (check-invocation-log-entry.sh:213,237). The slice's STATUS.md edit triggers the workflow; resolve-dispatch finds the DISPATCH-NOTE, slice_id 024B-extras-3 is not exempt, enforce=true, and the enforcer dies on cascade-status: not applicable without --allow-not-applicable.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"workflow yml:72–80 lists 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G; 024B-extras-3 absent. enforcer script:213,237 same allowlist. DISPATCH-NOTE line 8: 'cascade-status: not applicable'. Workflow passes no --allow-not-applicable flag (yml:101–105). enforcer script:198–199 dies if flag absent.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Immediate: CI check fails on the slice's own PR. Systemic: dual-maintenance surface means a future operator can add a new tooling slice to the workflow exempt list without updating the enforcer allowlist. Workflow then short-circuits (enforce=false) while the enforcer would have caught it — a workflow-side bypass path noted as FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001 but not resolved here.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add 024B-extras-3 to the workflow case statement (yml:72) and to the enforcer --tooling-slice-id allowlist (check-invocation-log-entry.sh:213,237). Add --allow-not-applicable --tooling-slice-id 024B-extras-3 to the workflow invocation for tooling-slice PRs, or add 024B-extras-3 to the workflow path-trigger short-circuit. Track the dual-maintenance surface explicitly until the workflow and enforcer use a single shared allowlist.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"enforce_admins.enabled in validate_restore_source_json() accepts int 0 and int 1 (enable-required-check.sh:459–463) while TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS in the same validator require isinstance(value, bool). A crafted pre-state with {enforce_admins: {enabled: 0}} passes validation and is coerced to false by transform(), silently bypassing the explicit rejection that identical treatment of toggle keys would produce.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:459–463: 'or (isinstance(enabled, int) and enabled in (0, 1))'. TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS loop at :491: 'if isinstance(value, bool): continue' — no int tolerance. The downstream bash guard at :1019 catches enforce_admins=false without ACK, so coercion does not escape into an unguarded apply.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"No confirmed bypass (downstream ACK gate catches it). Inconsistency means a future refactor removing the bash ACK gate would expose an unguarded int-as-false coercion path that disables admin enforcement. Also undermines the self-consistency claim of the hardening slice.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Remove the int 0/1 tolerance from enforce_admins.enabled validation and require isinstance(enabled, bool) consistently. Add a test asserting {enforce_admins: {enabled: 0}} is rejected with exit 2. This normalises the validator across all fields.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-MIN-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"transform() in validate_restore_source_json() has no else clause for the TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS branch (enable-required-check.sh:537–543). Any value that passes the validator but fails both transform conditions would be silently dropped from the PUT body rather than raising an error. Current conditions are logically equivalent so this is not reachable, but there is no assertion enforcing that equivalence.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:537–543: 'elif key in TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS: if ... out[key] = ...; elif isinstance(value, bool): out[key] = value' — no else clause. Validator at :487–509 exits 2 on any non-bool non-valid-dict value, so the silent-drop branch is unreachable in practice.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Not exploitable today. If a future edit widens the validator to accept a new shape (e.g., an int 0/1 tolerance analogous to enforce_admins) without updating the transform, the value would be silently dropped from the PUT body — restoring a permissive posture without an error signal.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add an else clause that calls sys.exit(2) with a diagnostic: 'should not reach here — validator precondition not met'. This makes the invariant explicit and prevents silent drop on any future validator/transform divergence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-MIN-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED is extracted via inline Python bool() coercion (enable-required-check.sh:968–970). A pre-state JSON with {required_signatures: {enabled: 'false'}} (non-empty string) passes the validator's (dict, type(None)) check and produces RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED=true, incorrectly scheduling a signatures-enable POST even though the operator intended to restore to a no-signatures state.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:969: \\\\\\\"enabled = bool(((data.get('required_signatures') or {}).get('enabled', False)))\\\\\\\". bool('false') == True (non-empty string). Validator at :428–430 accepts required_signatures as (dict, type(None)) with no enabled-field type check. The ACK guard at :971 only triggers when CURRENT=true AND RESTORE=false, so this inversion is unguarded.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Requires operator to supply a malformed pre-state file (real GitHub API always returns bool). If triggered, the restore incorrectly enables required_signatures on a repo that had them disabled, tightening posture unexpectedly without ACK. Not a bypass but a correctness inversion in the restore path.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Replace the inline bool() coercion with an isinstance check consistent with the TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS pattern: extract enabled = (data.get('required_signatures') or {}).get('enabled', False) and emit 'true' only if isinstance(enabled, bool) and enabled, otherwise 'false'. Add a test asserting {required_signatures: {enabled: 'false'}} produces RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED=false.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-NIT-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Toggle-validator rejection tests (cases a–e in test file:2490–2692) verify that stderr contains the field name but do not assert which error-message class is emitted (malformed-shape vs unexpected-type). If the two print() branches were swapped, all tests would still pass.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test file:2535: run_restore_case ... 2 '' 'lock_branch'. test file:2575: run_restore_case ... 2 '' 'allow_force_pushes'. Assertions check only for field name substring in stderr, not for 'malformed shape' or 'unexpected type' token.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Minimal. Both branches exit 2 and cite the field name, so the functional guard is present. An incorrect message class would confuse operators diagnosing a rejection but would not create a bypass.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a second grep assertion per case that verifies the expected message class token (e.g., 'malformed shape' for case-a and 'unexpected type' for cases c/d) is also present in stderr. This makes the diagnostic contract explicit and detects message-class regressions.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"overall_verdict\\\": \\\"FAIL\\\"\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"c0a90962-a6d3-433b-9217-4fadac329d0a\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.7243557,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":8,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":76132,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":251409,\"output_tokens\":24105,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":76132,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":3277,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":74653,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":9050,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":9050},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1729,\"outputTokens\":22,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0018390000000000001,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":8,\"outputTokens\":24105,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":251409,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":76132,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.7225167,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"c9377e58-0633-4c6e-95fc-f0529e08789e\"}\n\n---FILE---\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":365056,\"duration_api_ms\":365031,\"num_turns\":25,\"result\":\"```json\\n{\\n  \\\"reviewer\\\": \\\"sonnet-r1-completeness_governance\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"COMPLETENESS_GOVERNANCE\\\",\\n  \\\"slice\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-3\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"NOT_APPROVED\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Scope coverage is substantively correct: both TFs are named in the DISPATCH-NOTE, both are addressed in code, both are marked closed 2026-05-14 with slice reference in STATUS.md tracked-forward entries, and the 4-step chain entry is present. The validator hardening and workflow base-branch pin are delivered per spec. D-NNN omission framing is coherent under D-048. One MAJ blocks approval: the workflow's tooling-slice short-circuit case statement omits '024B-extras-3', meaning STATUS.md's presence in the PR diff triggers enforcement, the script sees 'cascade-status: not applicable' without --allow-not-applicable, and the check exits 2. Per TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001 the check is not yet required-status-checked on main, so this does not currently block merge, but the defect is governance-gap class (wrong enforcement path taken) and must be fixed before the check becomes required. Three MIN-class documentation gaps: (1) 'Last updated' annotation incorrectly says 'D-048 filed'—D-048 was filed in extras-2; (2) ACCEPTANCE-CHECKLIST row 5 says 'CLOSED across 3 sibling slices' but extras-3 is the 4th; (3) TF workflow-pin closure entry lacks a commit SHA. PR template / R1 evidence linkage (items 9–11) cannot be evaluated—no PR exists yet (checklist item 7 unchecked). Two nits on DISPATCH-NOTE accuracy. Anti-descoping: no third TF deferred; no silent descope detected.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Workflow tooling-slice short-circuit omits '024B-extras-3', causing check-invocation-log-entry to attempt enforcement on this very PR.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\".github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml resolve-dispatch step: 'case \\\\\\\"$slice_id\\\\\\\" in 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G)'. This PR modifies STATUS.md (a trigger path), causing the workflow to fire. The dispatch-note resolution grep matches docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-3/DISPATCH-NOTE.md, extracting slice_id='024B-extras-3'. Case falls through → enforce=true. Script sees 'cascade-status: not applicable' without --allow-not-applicable → exit 2 (confirmed by test case at line 1683 of test file).\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"CI check fails with 'ERROR: cascade-status: not applicable found, but --allow-not-applicable was not passed.' Currently advisory (TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001: check not yet required-status-checked on main), but represents a governance trail defect and blocks the slice when the check becomes required before 024C.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add '024B-extras-3' to the case-statement exclusion list in the resolve-dispatch step: 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024B-extras-3|024G. Symmetric with prior tooling-slice entries; one-line change.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"STATUS.md 'Last updated' annotation incorrectly states 'D-048 filed'—D-048 was filed in extras-2, not extras-3.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md line 3: '**Last updated:** 2026-05-14 (WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-3 defensive hardening; D-048 filed)'. DISPATCH-NOTE line 6 explicitly states 'Decision filed: None (no new D-NNN required—defensive hardening only; sits under D-048 umbrella)'. D-048 was filed at PR #114 (extras-2 merge).\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Future readers scanning the decision log to confirm when D-048 was filed will find the STATUS.md header misleadingly implies extras-3 did the filing. Low severity—DECISIONS.md is authoritative—but the header is the at-a-glance audit trail.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Correct the annotation to '2026-05-14 (WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-3 defensive hardening; 2 TFs closed; no new D-NNN)' or equivalent.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MIN-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"ACCEPTANCE-CHECKLIST row 5 shows 024B closed across 3 sibling slices; with extras-3 landing it should reflect the 4th sibling.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024A-plan-doc/ACCEPTANCE-CHECKLIST.md row 5 Status column: 'CLOSED across 3 sibling slices: 024B-core merged 249aa9f; 024B-extras-1 merged d7b16d0; 024B-extras-2 merged 13572fe'. Checklist header: 'Status as of: 2026-05-13 (post 024B-extras-2 merges)'. DISPATCH-NOTE line 61: 'After this slice, the 024B-extras chain (core + extras-1 + extras-2 + extras-3) is fully closed at the tooling-slice tier.'\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Governance audit: checklist row 5 understates 024B closure. When reviewed against DECISIONS.md (D-044/D-047/D-048 + no D-NNN for extras-3), the discrepancy is resolvable, but the checklist is the human-readable AC closure summary and should stay current.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update row 5 Status column to add '024B-extras-3 merged <SHA> 2026-05-14 (no new D-NNN; TF closures)' and advance 'Status as of' date to 2026-05-14.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MIN-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF closure entries lack the GREEN-phase implementation commit SHA; DISPATCH-NOTE scope table required 'slice + commit-SHA reference'.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md line 361 (TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TOGGLE-VALIDATOR-001): cites RED commit '744e4d1' but not GREEN implementation commit. STATUS.md line 370 (TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001): no commit SHA cited at all. DISPATCH-NOTE scope table row 'STATUS.md TF closure markers': 'Mark both TFs closed 2026-05-14 with slice + commit-SHA reference.' Git log shows GREEN phase at cdf6d49.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Future git-blame / audit trail will not have a direct commit SHA in the TF entry to diff against. Comparable closed entries (e.g. TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001) cite only 'per D-048', so this is consistent with prior practice; nevertheless the DISPATCH-NOTE's own scope spec required it.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Append 'GREEN implementation at cdf6d49' to both TF closure parenthetical. One-line edit per entry.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE scope table test count is ambiguous: '7 test cases asserting the validator rejects malformed toggle shapes + 2 no-regression guards' implies 9 total, but the actual file has 5 rejection + 2 no-regression = 7.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh around line 2490 (TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TOGGLE-VALIDATOR-001 section): cases (a)-(e) are rejection tests; (f)-(g) are no-regression guards. STATUS.md chain step 1 also says '7 new test cases' (counting all of a-g). DISPATCH-NOTE says '7 test cases asserting... + 2 no-regression guards'.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Inconsistent count across DISPATCH-NOTE / STATUS.md chain / test file. Does not affect correctness of delivered tests, which are adequate.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Correct DISPATCH-NOTE table to '5 rejection tests + 2 no-regression guards (7 total)' or align STATUS.md chain step 1 to match. Cosmetic.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"nit-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE slice opening checklist items 4–7 remain unchecked even though Codex implementation and R1 dispatch have completed.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE lines 68–71: items 4 (Codex dispatch), 5 (3-lens R1 review), 6 (fix-rounds), 7 (PR + self-merge) all show '[ ]'. Git log shows cdf6d49 (GREEN implementation) and git status shows r1-*.json files untracked (R1 in progress). Prior slices updated the checklist incrementally after each phase.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"The DISPATCH-NOTE serves as the slice's chain-of-custody document; unchecked items for completed phases make it look like neither implementation nor review have started, reducing future auditability.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Mark item 4 [x] after GREEN commit; mark item 5 [x] after R1 review completes and archive. Defer items 6 and 7 until fix-rounds and PR.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"abff42f6-5984-4b8e-aaab-636894db082a\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.9622147000000001,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1461,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":95236,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":970739,\"output_tokens\":20524,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":95236,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":3212,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":95134,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7673,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":7673},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1470,\"outputTokens\":29,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001615,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":1461,\"outputTokens\":20524,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":970739,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":95236,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.9605997000000002,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"05a5526e-0ae7-4e55-b3f1-1ad04ffa9f05\"}\n\n---FILE---\n# DISPATCH-NOTE — WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-extras-3 (defensive hardening)\n\n**Date:** 2026-05-14\n**Branch:** `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-3-validator-hardening` (off origin/main at `dbbebb5`)\n**Predecessor:** WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 merged at `13572fe` on 2026-05-13 (PR #114) + governance remediation PR #115 merged at `dbbebb5` 2026-05-13.\n**Decision filed:** None (no new D-NNN required — defensive hardening only; sits under D-048's depth-defense umbrella).\n\n`cascade-status: not applicable` — tooling slice; defensive hardening of existing depth-defense surface.\n`slice-type: tooling`\n\n## Backstory\n\nTwo TFs filed during 024B-extras-2 R-cycles remained open at merge time. Both are defensive-hardening items (not security bypasses); both are bounded engineering work; neither gates 024C. Closing them in a small sibling slice keeps the 024B-extras lineage cleanly chained.\n\n## Scope (in)\n\n| Deliverable | Path | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` validator hardening | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Extend the Python validator in `validate_restore_source_json()` to assert each `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` field (`required_linear_history`, `allow_force_pushes`, `allow_deletions`, `block_creations`, `required_conversation_resolution`, `lock_branch`, `allow_fork_syncing`) present in the pre-state JSON is EITHER `bool` OR a `dict` with `set(keys()) <= {\"enabled\", \"url\"}` AND `isinstance(value.get(\"enabled\"), bool)`. Raise with a clear diagnostic citing the offending field name on mismatch. Absent fields remain fine. Closes TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TOGGLE-VALIDATOR-001. |\n| Workflow base-branch pin | `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` | Invoke `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` from `origin/main` rather than PR HEAD. Pattern: `git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh > /tmp/check-invocation-log-entry.sh && bash /tmp/check-invocation-log-entry.sh ...` (the existing `actions/checkout@de0fac... with fetch-depth: 0` step already provides the `origin/main` ref). Closes TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001. |\n| RED-phase tests (committed first) | `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` | 7 test cases asserting the validator rejects malformed toggle shapes + 2 no-regression guards. Committed at `744e4d1` (RED). After implementation, tests go GREEN. |\n| STATUS.md TF closure markers | `STATUS.md` | Mark both TFs closed 2026-05-14 with slice + commit-SHA reference. |\n| STATUS.md chain entry | `STATUS.md` | 2026-05-14 chain entry recording the slice. |\n| DISPATCH-NOTE (this file) | `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-3/DISPATCH-NOTE.md` | Scope + checklist. |\n\n## Scope (out)\n\n- 024C PIM canary cascade — hard-gated on FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 (ACC-side, not SCP-side).\n- New D-NNN — defensive hardening under D-048 umbrella; no new doctrine surface.\n- Operator-attended residue (PAT rotation, throw-away repo cleanup, staging deploy) — hard environmental blockers.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] RED-phase tests committed first (TDD discipline)\n- [ ] Validator hardening: malformed toggle shapes rejected with exit 2 + clear diagnostic\n- [ ] Workflow base-branch pin: `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` invokes script from `origin/main` ref\n- [ ] All new tests pass (GREEN)\n- [ ] Existing tests still pass (no regression)\n- [ ] shellcheck clean on script + tests\n- [ ] 3-lens R1 review reached fixpoint at criterion (a) or (b)\n- [ ] STATUS.md TF closure markers + chain entry\n- [ ] PR + self-merge per D-040\n\n## Sequencing\n\n| Phase | Work | Mode | Wall |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | Pre-flight: branch off main; RED tests committed | Manual | done (744e4d1) |\n| 1 | Codex T3 single pass: validator hardening + workflow base-branch pin | Codex | ~15 min |\n| 2 | 3-lens R1 review | Sonnet | ~25-30 min |\n| 3 | Fix-rounds to fixpoint | Codex + Sonnet | ~1-2 hrs (expect ≤2 R-cycles given small surface) |\n| 4 | Self-merge + STATUS.md closures | Opus | ~10 min |\n\nTarget: 024B-extras-3 merged within ~2-3 hours wall-clock (small surface; advisory hardening).\n\n## Carry-forward TFs from extras-2 (status at slice opening)\n\n- TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TOGGLE-VALIDATOR-001 — **closes in this slice**\n- TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001 — **closes in this slice**\n\nNo other open TFs in the 024B-extras lineage. After this slice, the 024B-extras chain (core + extras-1 + extras-2 + extras-3) is fully closed at the tooling-slice tier.\n\n## Slice opening checklist\n\n- [x] DISPATCH-NOTE drafted (this file)\n- [x] Branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-3-validator-hardening` opened off main `dbbebb5`\n- [x] RED-phase tests committed (744e4d1)\n- [ ] Codex dispatch to implement validator hardening + workflow base-branch pin\n- [ ] 3-lens R1 review\n- [ ] Fix-rounds to fixpoint\n- [ ] PR + self-merge per D-040\n\nThis slice does NOT gate 024C. The cohort cascade remains hard-gated on FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 (ACC-side).\n\n---FILE---\n# WP-SCP-024 024A plan-doc acceptance checklist\n\n**Slice:** WP-SCP-024 024A (plan-doc landed at PR #102 / `4dc3faa` on 2026-05-04)\n**Status as of:** 2026-05-13 (post 024B-core + 024B-extras-1 + 024B-extras-2 merges)\n**Source:** `docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md` §6 (Slice plan) + §8 (Acceptance criteria + Threshold A)\n**Closes governance gap:** GAP-P1-002 (orchestrator audit, 2026-05-13) — plan-doc §6 acceptance criteria did not have an enumerated checklist with per-criterion disposition.\n\n## How to read this checklist\n\nEach row lists one of the 14 acceptance criteria spanning plan-doc §6 (per-slice ACs) and §8 (plan-doc level + Threshold A). Status values per criterion at PR #102 merge time vs. as of today (2026-05-13):\n\n- **CLOSED** — satisfied at the named slice merge (cited via `git log`-grade commit SHA).\n- **DEFERRED** — explicitly assigned to a later named slice; not in scope at PR #102 but tracked.\n- **N/A** — not applicable to this slice (e.g. a Threshold A criterion is not a plan-doc-merge criterion).\n\n`grep_production_before_planning.md`: each closure cites file:line or commit SHA so the claim is verifiable.\n\n## §8 plan-doc level acceptance (3 criteria)\n\n| # | Criterion | Status at PR #102 merge (2026-05-04) | Status as of 2026-05-13 | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | v0.1 plan-doc lands with §1–§10 populated | CLOSED | CLOSED | `docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md` §1 line 23 through §10 line 269 — all 10 sections populated; PR #102 merged at `4dc3faa` 2026-05-04 |\n| 2 | 3-lens R1+R2 fixpoint reached (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on a complete cycle) | CLOSED | CLOSED | 9 review rounds total per `project_wp_scp_024_plan.md` memory — longest in the WP-SCP-019/020/021/022/023/024 chain; 32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds; R9 returned 0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on a complete cycle |\n| 3 | D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reserved (not assigned in this slice) | CLOSED | D-044 FILED + D-045/D-046 STILL RESERVED | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-044 row (line 100) ratifies 024B-core operational contracts — accepted 2026-05-09. D-045 (024C) and D-046 (024G) remain reserved per the DECISIONS.md header reservation note |\n\n## §6 per-slice acceptance criteria (7 slices)\n\n| # | Slice | Criterion | Status at PR #102 merge | Status as of 2026-05-13 | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 4 | 024A | Plan-doc R2 fixpoint reached + merged | CLOSED | CLOSED | This slice; PR #102 / `4dc3faa` |\n| 5 | 024B | Scaffolder emits known-fixture wrapper; CI script implements all 4 cascade-status behaviours; D-044 filed; `--restore` + ADOPT-001 §12.8 + workflow wiring ship | DEFERRED (split per `D-SCP-024B-SCOPE-SPLIT-2026-05-09.md`) | CLOSED across 3 sibling slices: 024B-core merged `249aa9f` 2026-05-09 (D-044); 024B-extras-1 merged `d7b16d0` 2026-05-12 (D-047, PR #113); 024B-extras-2 merged `13572fe` 2026-05-13 (D-048, PR #114) |\n| 6 | 024C | PIM `policy-check / scp/policy-check` required-check live; ≥1 Renovate-bump-propagation cycle merged clean; D-045 filed | DEFERRED | DEFERRED — gated on FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 (ACC-side, not SCP-side). Pre-staged at `/tmp/codex-wp/scp/024c-kickoff-prep/` per `project_wp_scp_024_plan.md` |\n| 7 | 024D | control-tower `policy-check / scp/policy-check` required-check live; ≥1 Renovate-bump-propagation cycle merged clean | DEFERRED | DEFERRED — opens after 024C bake-clean (canary-first per §5.1) |\n| 8 | 024E | mapp-doc-agent + recommender paired cascade — both adopters' required-checks live; ≥1 Renovate-bump-propagation cycle merged clean on each | DEFERRED | DEFERRED — opens after 024D bake-clean |\n| 9 | 024F | shopify-app `policy-check / scp/policy-check` required-check live; ≥1 Renovate-bump-propagation cycle merged clean | DEFERRED | DEFERRED — opens after 024E bake-clean |\n| 10 | 024G | ≥3 cohort adopters onboarded + bake-clean + USER-GATE-E signed; D-046 filed | DEFERRED | DEFERRED — closing slice; opens when ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters have all sibling §8 Threshold A criteria satisfied |\n\n## §8 Threshold A criteria (4 mandatory)\n\nThreshold A is the binary pass/fail closure gate for WP-SCP-024 as a whole. At PR #102 merge (plan-doc), Threshold A criteria are by definition all DEFERRED. Each criterion below names the slice or operational state where it closes.\n\n| # | Criterion | Status at PR #102 merge | Status as of 2026-05-13 | Evidence / Closure path |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 11 | ≥3 of {PIM, recommender, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower, shopify-app} have `policy-check / scp/policy-check` as a required status check on default branch | DEFERRED | DEFERRED (0 of 5 onboarded) | Closes incrementally via 024C–024F adopter slices; counted at 024G |\n| 12 | Each onboarded adopter has a corresponding entry in `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` with operator + timestamp + before/after API JSON + script SHA256 + git SHA — OR is `cascade-status: blocked-on-adopter-conflict` with the matching TF | DEFERRED | DEFERRED | Logged per-cascade-slice; verified at 024G |\n| 13 | Each onboarded adopter has survived ≥1 SCP minor version-bump cycle propagated cleanly via Renovate (Renovate-issued PR merged + observed clean on default branch); operator-driven R-024-07 bumps do NOT count toward Threshold A | DEFERRED | DEFERRED | Per-adopter bake captured in cascade slice STATUS.md row; gated on Renovate's per-adopter cadence |\n| 14 | USER-GATE-E artefact (`docs/gates/USER-GATE-E.md`) signed by @jrnb2024 | DEFERRED | DEFERRED | Operator action at 024G close; `docs/gates/USER-GATE-E.md` scaffolded but unsigned until criteria 11–13 close |\n\n## Summary\n\nAt PR #102 merge (2026-05-04):\n- **CLOSED:** 4 of 14 (criteria 1, 2, 3, 4 — all plan-doc level).\n- **DEFERRED:** 10 of 14 (criteria 5–14 — all implementation-slice or Threshold A level).\n\nAs of 2026-05-13 (post 024B-extras-2 merge):\n- **CLOSED:** 5 of 14 (criteria 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 — plan-doc + all of 024B fully delivered via 3-sibling split).\n- **DEFERRED:** 9 of 14 (criteria 6–14 — cascade implementation slices + Threshold A; 024C blocked by FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001, downstream slices gated on canary-first sequencing).\n\n## Cross-references\n\n- `docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md` §6 (Slice plan) + §8 (Acceptance criteria + Threshold A) — canonical AC source.\n- `docs/decisions/D-SCP-024B-SCOPE-SPLIT-2026-05-09.md` — operator-decided 024B split (closes GAP-P1-001).\n- `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-044 (024B-core), D-047 (024B-extras-1), D-048 (024B-extras-2) — implementation ratifications.\n- `STATUS.md` \"Open scheduled follow-ups\" + tracked-forward section — outstanding TFs per slice.\n\n## Maintenance\n\nThis checklist is informational. The canonical AC source is the plan-doc itself; this file mirrors the AC enumeration in checklist form with per-criterion disposition for governance-audit consumption. Update when a deferred criterion closes (cite the slice's PR + commit SHA in the Status column).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
