{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '60,110p' .github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml && printf '\\\\n---FILE---\\\\n' && sed -n '340,390p' STATUS.md && printf '\\\\n---FILE---\\\\n' && sed -n '198,210p' STATUS.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n          # Prefer cohort slices (024C-024F) over tooling slices so a\n          # mixed PR cannot short-circuit enforcement on the wrong note.\n          cohort_dispatch_note=\"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$all_dispatch_notes\" | grep -E '^docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-F]/DISPATCH-NOTE.md$' | head -n1 || true)\"\n          if [ -n \"$cohort_dispatch_note\" ]; then\n            dispatch_note=\"$cohort_dispatch_note\"\n          else\n            dispatch_note=\"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$all_dispatch_notes\" | head -n1)\"\n          fi\n\n          slice_id=\"$(basename \"$(dirname \"$dispatch_note\")\")\"\n          case \"$slice_id\" in\n            024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G)\n              if [ \"$log_modified_count\" -gt 0 ]; then\n                echo 'ERROR: branch-protection-log.md must not be modified in a tooling-slice PR' >&2\n                exit 1\n              fi\n              echo \"Tooling slice ($slice_id); no enforcement needed.\"\n              printf 'enforce=false\\n' >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n              exit 0\n              ;;\n          esac\n          printf 'enforce=true\\n' >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n          printf 'dispatch_note=%s\\n' \"$dispatch_note\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n      - name: Check invocation log entry\n        if: steps.resolve-dispatch.outputs.enforce == 'true'\n        shell: bash\n        env:\n          dispatch_note: ${{ steps.resolve-dispatch.outputs.dispatch_note }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          # Pin enforcement to the base-branch (origin/main) version of the\n          # script rather than the PR HEAD copy. Closes\n          # TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001: an attacker-modified\n          # PR could otherwise substitute a no-op enforcement script and\n          # bypass the gate. The actions/checkout step above runs with\n          # fetch-depth: 0 so origin/main is available locally.\n          enforcer_script=\"$(mktemp)\"\n          trap 'rm -f \"$enforcer_script\"' EXIT\n          git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh > \"$enforcer_script\"\n          bash \"$enforcer_script\" \\\n            --diff-base origin/main \\\n            --dispatch-note \"$dispatch_note\" \\\n            --status-md STATUS.md \\\n            --branch-protection-log docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\n\n---FILE---\n- ~~**020E.c**: waiver-suppression canary + `scripts/replay-canary.sh`~~ ✅ landed 2026-04-30 (PR #70, commit `4962bc9`); needed 2-PR fixpoint dance for warn-msg conftest bug.\n- ~~**020F**: Renovate shared preset~~ ✅ landed 2026-04-30 (PR #71, commit `2743d4a`); 4-round R1 fixpoint surfaced CRIT-SAFE-001 (renovate/v* unprotected) → D-034 + new ruleset live; preset published at `renovate/v1.0.0`.\n- ~~**020G**: branch-protection automation script for adopter onboarding~~ ✅ landed 2026-04-30 (PR #74, commit `373bcd2`); fix-round-1 closed 11 R1 findings + R2 + R3 + R4 fixpoint.\n- ~~**020H part 3**: ADOPT-001 §12 federation-integration appendix (closes TF-D1-001..003)~~ ✅ landed 2026-04-30 (PR #75, commit `347fde2`); 6-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R3 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on all 3 lenses), 11 MAJ + 31 MIN + 11 nit closed. Opened TF-020H3-001..005.\n- ~~**020H.1**: VERSIONING.md + rule-RFC process + rollback detection + version-manifest.json + freshness-warning emit~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #78, commit `06c2b61`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on all 3 lenses), 6 MAJ + 17 MIN + 11 nit closed. Filed D-036 + opened TF-020H1-001..005. Closed SCP-073.sec (SECURITY.md published).\n- ~~**020H.2**: Regal binary SHA256 verification — closes TF-020H3-001~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #77, commit `bac1427`); 3-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ), 3 MAJ + 5 MIN + 13 nit closed; closed 13 days ahead of the 2026-05-14 deadline.\n- ~~**020H.3**: release-gate workflow (closes TF-005 + TF-020H1-001)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #79, commit `42f49db`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on all 3 lenses), 1 CRIT + 7 MAJ + 10 MIN + 10 nit closed across 2 fix-rounds. Architectural framing: workflow is observer/annotator (post-tag), not pre-emptive gate; pre-emptive enforcement is the operator's mandatory dry-run pre-flight discipline. Opened TF-020H3rg-001..003.\n- ~~**020H.3.1**: release-gate auto-issue (closes TF-020H3rg-003)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #80, commit `d3e3c73`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 with R2 safety clean APPROVED (0 findings), 1 MAJ + 8 MIN + 6 nit + 1 fix-round-1 self-correction closed. Two-job split: release-gate (contents:read) + release-gate-violation-issue (issues:write at job level per D-037). Filed TF-020H3rg-004.\n- ~~**020H.4**: rule-config disable canary (closes TF-020H1-004)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #82, commit `c67a91a`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on all 3 lenses), 1 MAJ + 6 MIN + 8 nit closed. New `canary/rule-config-disabled` branch (PR #81 DO-NOT-MERGE; SHA `841d350`) verified PASS at workflow run `25211284467`; `scripts/replay-canary.sh` registry extended; `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/canary-evidence.md` Canary 4 baseline section added. Suppression-path coverage triad complete (deny / waiver / rule-config). Opened TF-020H4-001..003.\n- ~~**SCP-073.sec**: `SECURITY.md` publication (security disclosure path for policy-bypass reports)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 in 020H.1 fix-round-1 (commit `3817384`); `SECURITY.md` at repo root with GitHub Security Advisory + `jimbrooke@me.com` channels, 3-business-day SLA, 30-day coordinated-disclosure target; ADOPT-001 §12.7.8 + `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/rule-regression.md` updated to reference it directly. Closes WP-SCP-020 §4.1 SCP-073.sec forward-looking flag.\n- ~~**TF-020H3rg-002**: pip install --require-hashes for both YAML/JSON-validating workflows~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-02 in slice 020M (PR #84, commit `0e24cc6`); cut v1.0.1 PATCH.\n- ~~**WP-SCP-022 proposal-queue**: structured proposal queue for new rules.~~ ✅ Phase 1 closed 2026-05-02 in slice **020L** (PR #89, commit `25db685`) — RFC-001 / SCP-R-004 (waiver `reason` must cite issue/PR URL) authored, R1+R2 fixpoint, merged via operator-discretion early-merge per D-040. ✅ **Phase 2** closed 2026-05-02 in slice **020P** (PR #91, commit `d83ce52`) — `policies/SCP-R-004.rego` + 21 Conftest tests + conflict-gate fixtures + workflow warn-baseline rendering + ADOPT-001 §12.7.14 + RULE-TEMPLATE.md §5 + README.md §3 amendments + **v1.1.0 tag cut** (`https://github.com/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/releases/tag/v1.1.0`). Closes TF-020L-002 + TF-020L-003. Filed TF-020P-001/002/003/004/005.\n- **WP-SCP-023**: cross-repo scorecards.\n- **WP-SCP-024**: estate cascade (FLA pilot → PIM/recommender/etc.).\n\n## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras\n\n- **FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001** (open): per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC. install_acc_hook.sh currently hardcodes ROOT_DIR via BASH_SOURCE so each adopter repo would need its own install ceremony. 024C MUST NOT open until closed. ACC-side work item; SCP-side awaits closure. Owner: @jrnb2024.\n- **FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001** (closed in fix-round-4; this commit): 024B-extras workflow wiring now skips script invocation entirely for tooling slices, so the residual operator-supplied `not applicable` bypass surface is gone without passing `--allow-not-applicable` or `--tooling-slice-id` into the script. Cohort cascade slices still invoke the script with full enforcement; defense-in-depth now comes from the workflow short-circuit plus the script's default refusal of `--allow-not-applicable`.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): add per-test coverage for `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh` target-selection loop in 024B-extras-2 (or a future slice). The loop now has 2 path-based excludes (`tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` + the narrowed `docs/reviews/*/r1-*.json` + siblings); `run_workflow_guard_case` now exercises 024B-extras-2 tooling short-circuiting, 024D/024E/024F cohort enforcement, and 024G tooling short-circuiting. Surfaced by R23 fix-round-23 + R24 review of fix-round-24. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): extend PUT-body shape assertions (`jq -e 'has($field) and .[$field] | type == \"boolean\"'` pattern) across ALL existing restore test cases in `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh`. Added strict PUT-body shape assertions to `restore-checks-canonical`, `restore-checks-wrong-context-ack`, and `restore-log-sanitization` during this fix-round. Surfaced by step-7 demo + R22 + R25 against real GitHub API (the 3rd mock-masking CRIT in this slice's history). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TOGGLE-VALIDATOR-001** (closed 2026-05-14: implemented in 024B-extras-3; validator hardening added in `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` and RED tests were committed first at `744e4d1`): `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` handler in `validate_restore_source_json()` silently drops fields with non-conforming shape (e.g. an unexpected `{enabled, url, foo}` keyset). The Python validator does NOT check toggle-field shapes — future GitHub API drift introducing a new toggle field with extra metadata would silently omit the field from PUT body with no operator error. Closure: extend the Python validator to assert each `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` field is either `bool` or a `dict` with `set(value.keys()) <= {\"enabled\", \"url\"}` (matching the handler's accept set); raise on mismatch. Defensive hardening; not a security bypass (drop-on-mismatch is fail-safe). Owner: 024B-extras-3 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): `validate_restore_source_json()` `transform()` uses an exclusion-list approach — unknown GitHub branch-protection fields pass through to the PUT body. R30 surfaced `lock_branch`, `required_linear_history`, `block_creations` (and any future similar) pass through with NO posture-degradation guard, allowing a malicious pre-state to enable these without operator ack. Closure: switch to inclusion-list transform (explicitly allowed fields) + posture-degradation acknowledgement flags for each guarded sub-field. Aligns with the depth-defense surface carve (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (D-048); does NOT gate 024C — current exclusion list is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO since cohort pre-states are operator-captured from REAL adopter GET (not attacker-crafted).\n- **TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001** (closed 2026-05-11): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7 completed against `jrnb2024/scp-024b-extras-restore-test` throw-away repo. **Surfaced CRIT** (mock-masking: transform did not unwrap `*.enabled` sub-objects for `required_linear_history`/`allow_force_pushes`/etc → HTTP 422 on real PUT); closed in fix-round-22 with generic `{enabled: bool}` unwrap + PUT-body-shape assertion test. Round-trip succeeded post-fix; all 4 key fields matched state-A target. Throw-away repo cleanup deferred — current gh token lacks `delete_repo` scope.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): apply `resolve_inside_repo_root()` guard to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <path>` argument in 024B-extras-2 alongside other defensive hardening. Low blast-radius (operator-credentials-bound). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001** (open): widen `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` cohort regex from `024[C-F]/` to `024[C-F][^/]*/` for future multi-char cohort slice IDs. Current 5-cohort set (024C/D/E/F) is single-char and unaffected; defensive. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001** (open): align DISPATCH-NOTE step-7 fixture sequence with `restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md` (add or harmonise `Mutate branch protection` step description). Will be resolved naturally at step-7 demo execution time.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): add test case for staged-but-uncommitted prior-restore evidence in 024B-extras-2 tests (guards against future narrowing of `git diff HEAD` to `git diff`). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): restore verify-phase set-equality comparison (deferred from 024B-extras-1 carve per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`). Closure: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` verify phase uses jq sorted-set comparison for `required_status_checks.contexts`. NOT BLOCKING 024C — extras-1's substring grep -F is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO. Owns: 024B-extras-2 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` reads RESTORE_PRE_STATE file once, then validates and extracts `required_signatures` from the captured in-memory JSON via stdin. Defensive hardening; current posture-degradation flag gates bound the blast radius. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001** (closed 2026-05-14: implemented in 024B-extras-3; workflow now pins execution to `origin/main` script content before invoking it): `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` from the PR's checked-out code (PR HEAD), not the base branch. For future multi-operator adoption, pin enforcement to `git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh | bash -s -- ...` or use a reusable workflow from base. Owner: 024B-extras-3 slice (depth-defense); does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001** (open): Before 024C dispatch opens, operator must add `check-invocation-log-entry / check-invocation-log-entry` to main branch's `required_status_checks` list via `gh api -X PATCH repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/branches/main/protection` with the updated contexts list, then record the SCP-self REQCHECK enablement as a `STATUS.md` chain entry only. Do NOT modify `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`; that log is reserved for adopter-side `enable-required-check.sh` invocations per D-035 scope. Without this step CI-enforcement is advisory only (the workflow runs but doesn't block merge). Close as part of 024C kickoff ceremony.\n- **TF-024B-SCAFFOLDER-023E002-UPDATE** (open): when TF-023E-002 closes, remove the post-v1.2.0 warning block from `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` and delete the cutover ancestry guard that keeps the v1.0.0 fallback recommendation alive. The scaffolder should stop warning only after the separate `attest-scorecard` workflow restructuring lands. Owner: @jrnb2024.\n\n---FILE---\n\n## Today's chain (2026-05-14 — 024B-extras-3 defensive hardening)\n\n| Step | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-3-validator-hardening` off main `dbbebb5`. RED-phase tests committed first (`744e4d1`) per TDD discipline - 7 new test cases asserting validator rejects malformed `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` shapes. |\n| 2 | Codex T3 implementation - validator hardening in `validate_restore_source_json()` + workflow base-branch pin in `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`. |\n| 3 | GREEN - all new tests pass; existing tests unchanged; shellcheck clean. |\n| 4 | TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TOGGLE-VALIDATOR-001 + TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001 closed; 024B-extras chain now fully closed at tooling-slice tier. |\n\n## Open PRs (post-Threshold-A session close-out)\n\n- **PR #59** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/deliberate-violation-pre`; permanent fixture; CI=FAIL by design (deny); blocked structurally by required-check.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
