{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba STATUS.md | sed -n '198,214p' && printf '\\\\n---FILE---\\\\n' && nl -ba STATUS.md | sed -n '356,377p'\"","aggregated_output":"   198\t\n   199\t## Today's chain (2026-05-14 — 024B-extras-3 defensive hardening)\n   200\t\n   201\t| Step | Notes |\n   202\t|---|---|\n   203\t| 1 | Branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-3-validator-hardening` off main `dbbebb5`. RED-phase tests committed first (`744e4d1`) per TDD discipline - 7 new test cases asserting validator rejects malformed `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` shapes. |\n   204\t| 2 | Codex T3 implementation - validator hardening in `validate_restore_source_json()` + workflow base-branch pin in `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`. |\n   205\t| 3 | GREEN - all new tests pass; existing tests unchanged; shellcheck clean. |\n   206\t| 4 | TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TOGGLE-VALIDATOR-001 + TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001 closed; filed TF-024B-EXTRAS-3-ENFORCE-ADMINS-VALIDATOR-001 + TF-024B-EXTRAS-3-SIGNATURES-EXTRACT-VALIDATOR-001 (open, filed 2026-05-14); GREEN implementation at cdf6d49. |\n   207\t\n   208\t## Open PRs (post-Threshold-A session close-out)\n   209\t\n   210\t- **PR #59** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/deliberate-violation-pre`; permanent fixture; CI=FAIL by design (deny); blocked structurally by required-check.\n   211\t- **PR #67** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/waived-violation`; permanent fixture; CI=PASS via waiver suppression; label-only protection (TF-020H4-002 covers).\n   212\t- **PR #81** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/rule-config-disabled`; permanent fixture; CI=PASS via rule-config suppression; label-only protection (TF-020H4-002 covers).\n   213\t- **Dependabot PRs**: ✅ all 4 stale MAJOR-version Action bumps cleared 2026-05-02. setup-python (#72), upload-artifact (#44), download-artifact (#42), checkout (#43) — all merged after CI-green verification on rebased branches.\n   214\t\n\n---FILE---\n   356\t\n   357\t- **FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001** (open): per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC. install_acc_hook.sh currently hardcodes ROOT_DIR via BASH_SOURCE so each adopter repo would need its own install ceremony. 024C MUST NOT open until closed. ACC-side work item; SCP-side awaits closure. Owner: @jrnb2024.\n   358\t- **FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001** (closed in fix-round-4; this commit): 024B-extras workflow wiring now skips script invocation entirely for tooling slices, so the residual operator-supplied `not applicable` bypass surface is gone without passing `--allow-not-applicable` or `--tooling-slice-id` into the script. Cohort cascade slices still invoke the script with full enforcement; defense-in-depth now comes from the workflow short-circuit plus the script's default refusal of `--allow-not-applicable`.\n   359\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): add per-test coverage for `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh` target-selection loop in 024B-extras-2 (or a future slice). The loop now has 2 path-based excludes (`tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` + the narrowed `docs/reviews/*/r1-*.json` + siblings); `run_workflow_guard_case` now exercises 024B-extras-2 tooling short-circuiting, 024D/024E/024F cohort enforcement, and 024G tooling short-circuiting. Surfaced by R23 fix-round-23 + R24 review of fix-round-24. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n   360\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): extend PUT-body shape assertions (`jq -e 'has($field) and .[$field] | type == \"boolean\"'` pattern) across ALL existing restore test cases in `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh`. Added strict PUT-body shape assertions to `restore-checks-canonical`, `restore-checks-wrong-context-ack`, and `restore-log-sanitization` during this fix-round. Surfaced by step-7 demo + R22 + R25 against real GitHub API (the 3rd mock-masking CRIT in this slice's history). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n   361\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TOGGLE-VALIDATOR-001** (closed 2026-05-14: implemented in 024B-extras-3; validator hardening added in `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` and RED tests were committed first at `744e4d1`; GREEN implementation at cdf6d49): `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` handler in `validate_restore_source_json()` silently drops fields with non-conforming shape (e.g. an unexpected `{enabled, url, foo}` keyset). The Python validator does NOT check toggle-field shapes — future GitHub API drift introducing a new toggle field with extra metadata would silently omit the field from PUT body with no operator error. Closure: extend the Python validator to assert each `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` field is either `bool` or a `dict` with `set(value.keys()) <= {\"enabled\", \"url\"}` (matching the handler's accept set); raise on mismatch. Defensive hardening; not a security bypass (drop-on-mismatch is fail-safe). Owner: 024B-extras-3 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\n   362\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-3-ENFORCE-ADMINS-VALIDATOR-001** (open, filed 2026-05-14): `validate_restore_source_json()` in `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` accepts `enforce_admins.enabled` as int 0 or int 1 in addition to bool. GitHub's GET API returns bool consistently; the int tolerance is pre-existing slack that could mask real validator bugs. Surfaced by 024B-extras-3 R1 SB-MIN-001. Closure: tighten validator to `isinstance(enabled, bool)` only; add test asserting `{enforce_admins: {enabled: 0}}` rejected. Defensive hardening; symmetric with TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS strictness. Owner: 024B-extras-3 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\n   363\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-3-SIGNATURES-EXTRACT-VALIDATOR-001** (open, filed 2026-05-14): RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED extraction in `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` uses inline `bool()` coercion that would treat string 'false' (non-empty) as truthy. The validator's required_signatures check (`(dict, type(None))`) doesn't constrain the inner `enabled` field type. Pre-existing; not introduced by this slice. Surfaced by 024B-extras-3 R1 SB-MIN-003. Closure: replace `bool()` coercion with `isinstance` check; emit clear diagnostic on malformed nested type. Does NOT gate 024C.\n   364\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): `validate_restore_source_json()` `transform()` uses an exclusion-list approach — unknown GitHub branch-protection fields pass through to the PUT body. R30 surfaced `lock_branch`, `required_linear_history`, `block_creations` (and any future similar) pass through with NO posture-degradation guard, allowing a malicious pre-state to enable these without operator ack. Closure: switch to inclusion-list transform (explicitly allowed fields) + posture-degradation acknowledgement flags for each guarded sub-field. Aligns with the depth-defense surface carve (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (D-048); does NOT gate 024C — current exclusion list is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO since cohort pre-states are operator-captured from REAL adopter GET (not attacker-crafted).\n   365\t- **TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001** (closed 2026-05-11): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7 completed against `jrnb2024/scp-024b-extras-restore-test` throw-away repo. **Surfaced CRIT** (mock-masking: transform did not unwrap `*.enabled` sub-objects for `required_linear_history`/`allow_force_pushes`/etc → HTTP 422 on real PUT); closed in fix-round-22 with generic `{enabled: bool}` unwrap + PUT-body-shape assertion test. Round-trip succeeded post-fix; all 4 key fields matched state-A target. Throw-away repo cleanup deferred — current gh token lacks `delete_repo` scope.\n   366\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): apply `resolve_inside_repo_root()` guard to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <path>` argument in 024B-extras-2 alongside other defensive hardening. Low blast-radius (operator-credentials-bound). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n   367\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001** (open): widen `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` cohort regex from `024[C-F]/` to `024[C-F][^/]*/` for future multi-char cohort slice IDs. Current 5-cohort set (024C/D/E/F) is single-char and unaffected; defensive. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n   368\t- **TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001** (open): align DISPATCH-NOTE step-7 fixture sequence with `restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md` (add or harmonise `Mutate branch protection` step description). Will be resolved naturally at step-7 demo execution time.\n   369\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): add test case for staged-but-uncommitted prior-restore evidence in 024B-extras-2 tests (guards against future narrowing of `git diff HEAD` to `git diff`). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice.\n   370\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): restore verify-phase set-equality comparison (deferred from 024B-extras-1 carve per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`). Closure: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` verify phase uses jq sorted-set comparison for `required_status_checks.contexts`. NOT BLOCKING 024C — extras-1's substring grep -F is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO. Owns: 024B-extras-2 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\n   371\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` reads RESTORE_PRE_STATE file once, then validates and extracts `required_signatures` from the captured in-memory JSON via stdin. Defensive hardening; current posture-degradation flag gates bound the blast radius. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n   372\t- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001** (closed 2026-05-14: implemented in 024B-extras-3; GREEN implementation at cdf6d49; workflow now pins execution to `origin/main` script content before invoking it): `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` from the PR's checked-out code (PR HEAD), not the base branch. For future multi-operator adoption, pin enforcement to `git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh | bash -s -- ...` or use a reusable workflow from base. Owner: 024B-extras-3 slice (depth-defense); does NOT gate 024C.\n   373\t- **TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001** (open): Before 024C dispatch opens, operator must add `check-invocation-log-entry / check-invocation-log-entry` to main branch's `required_status_checks` list via `gh api -X PATCH repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/branches/main/protection` with the updated contexts list, then record the SCP-self REQCHECK enablement as a `STATUS.md` chain entry only. Do NOT modify `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`; that log is reserved for adopter-side `enable-required-check.sh` invocations per D-035 scope. Without this step CI-enforcement is advisory only (the workflow runs but doesn't block merge). Close as part of 024C kickoff ceremony.\n   374\t- **TF-024B-SCAFFOLDER-023E002-UPDATE** (open): when TF-023E-002 closes, remove the post-v1.2.0 warning block from `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` and delete the cutover ancestry guard that keeps the v1.0.0 fallback recommendation alive. The scaffolder should stop warning only after the separate `attest-scorecard` workflow restructuring lands. Owner: @jrnb2024.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
