XTRAS-3-SIGNATURES-EXTRACT-VALIDATOR-001** (open, filed 2026-05-14): RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED extraction in `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` uses inline `bool()` coercion that would treat string 'false' (non-empty) as truthy. The validator's required_signatures check (`(dict, type(None))`) doesn't constrain the inner `enabled` field type. Pre-existing; not introduced by this slice. Surfaced by 024B-extras-3 R1 SB-MIN-003. Closure: replace `bool()` coercion with `isinstance` check; emit clear diagnostic on malformed nested type. Does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:372:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001** (closed 2026-05-14: implemented in 024B-extras-3; GREEN implementation at cdf6d49; workflow now pins execution to `origin/main` script content before invoking it): `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` from the PR's checked-out code (PR HEAD), not the base branch. For future multi-operator adoption, pin enforcement to `git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh | bash -s -- ...` or use a reusable workflow from base. Owner: 024B-extras-3 slice (depth-defense); does NOT gate 024C.\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:207:        024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024B-extras-3|024G)\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:1712:  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 2 '' 'ERROR: --allow-not-applicable requires --tooling-slice-id <id> where <id> ∈ {024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024B-extras-2, 024B-extras-3, 024G}' \"\" --allow-not-applicable\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:1741:  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 2 '' 'ERROR: --allow-not-applicable requires --tooling-slice-id <id> where <id> ∈ {024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024B-extras-2, 024B-extras-3, 024G}' \"\" --allow-not-applicable --tooling-slice-id 024C\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:2537:  grep -Fq -- 'malformed shape' \"$LAST_RUN_