e field from PUT body with no operator error. Closure: extend the Python validator to assert each `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` field is either `bool` or a `dict` with `set(value.keys()) <= {\"enabled\", \"url\"}` (matching the handler's accept set); raise on mismatch. Defensive hardening; not a security bypass (drop-on-mismatch is fail-safe). Owner: 024B-extras-3 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\n+- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-3-ENFORCE-ADMINS-VALIDATOR-001** (open, filed 2026-05-14): `validate_restore_source_json()` in `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` accepts `enforce_admins.enabled` as int 0 or int 1 in addition to bool. GitHub's GET API returns bool consistently; the int tolerance is pre-existing slack that could mask real validator bugs. Surfaced by 024B-extras-3 R1 SB-MIN-001. Closure: tighten validator to `isinstance(enabled, bool)` only; add test asserting `{enforce_admins: {enabled: 0}}` rejected. Defensive hardening; symmetric with TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS strictness. Owner: 024B-extras-3 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\n+- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-3-SIGNATURES-EXTRACT-VALIDATOR-001** (open, filed 2026-05-14): RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED extraction in `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` uses inline `bool()` coercion that would treat string 'false' (non-empty) as truthy. The validator's required_signatures check (`(dict, type(None))`) doesn't constrain the inner `enabled` field type. Pre-existing; not introduced by this slice. Surfaced by 024B-extras-3 R1 SB-MIN-003. Closure: replace `bool()` coercion with `isinstance` check; emit clear diagnostic on malformed nested type. Does NOT gate 024C.\n - **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): `validate_restore_source_json()` `transform()` uses an exclusion-list approach — unknown GitHub branch-protection fields pass through to the PUT body. R30 surfaced `lock_branch`, `required_linear_history`, `block_creations` (and any future similar) pass through with NO posture-degradation guard